<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Khan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Khan was the supreme ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>, elected by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurultai">kurultai</a> of the Genghisid princes. After the empire fragmented, the title was held by Kublai and his successors of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>, whose nominal supremacy was recognised to varying degrees by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Khanate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-khan.jpg" alt="Great Khan" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giorgiomonteforti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperoryuandinastycollage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
